WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.140 --> 00:00:06.839
The big political story over the last 24 hours,
Bernie Sanders has suspended his 2020 Democratic

00:00:06.839 --> 00:00:11.880
presidential campaign.
There's just so much to talk about. And I've

00:00:11.880 --> 00:00:17.689
received hundreds of messages since yesterday
about this. Emails, tweets, all sorts of other

00:00:17.689 --> 00:00:23.300
messages, Instagram. And so I want to go through
this in sections. I want to make sure we cover

00:00:23.300 --> 00:00:27.230
everything. I want to make sure we sort of
turn over every stone that needs to be turned

00:00:27.230 --> 00:00:31.359
over in thinking about this and and going
forward. And so we're going to talk about

00:00:31.359 --> 00:00:37.030
Bernie's decision itself and whether it made
sense. We'll talk about what exactly happened

00:00:37.030 --> 00:00:41.579
in the campaign that at one point seemed to
be going so well. We'll talk about what this

00:00:41.579 --> 00:00:47.030
means for the progressive movement and for
the future of who the individuals are that

00:00:47.030 --> 00:00:51.469
may be leading. That movement will talk eventually.
We also have to talk about what this means

00:00:51.469 --> 00:00:54.980
for November of 2020.
So we're going to get to all of those things

00:00:54.980 --> 00:01:03.769
now. My concerns from the messages I've received
are centered around, I guess generally that

00:01:03.769 --> 00:01:08.921
a lot of these different issues I mentioned
are being mixed up. For example, there are

00:01:08.921 --> 00:01:15.509
people mixing up questions about the future
of the movement with November of 2020 when

00:01:15.509 --> 00:01:19.799
there is overlap, but really there are different
decisions and different considerations to

00:01:19.799 --> 00:01:22.920
be made there.
And it's leading to some unclear thinking

00:01:22.920 --> 00:01:27.000
and people that I think are are not thinking
in the clearest terms about this. And I want

00:01:27.000 --> 00:01:32.369
to make sure that if if nothing else, we can
disagree about where we end up. But let's

00:01:32.369 --> 00:01:37.560
make sure we have all of the facts and that
we're thinking clearly and discretely about

00:01:37.560 --> 00:01:42.759
all of these issues. If we come to different
conclusions, that's fine. I have no problem.

00:01:42.759 --> 00:01:47.600
We're adults. But let's think through the
different elements of this. First of all,

00:01:47.600 --> 00:01:52.520
here is Bernie himself saying yesterday that
he is suspending his campaign.

00:01:52.520 --> 00:01:58.649
I wish I could give you better news, but I
think you know the truth, and that is that

00:01:58.649 --> 00:02:05.130
we are now some 300 delegates behind Vise
President Biden, and the path toward victory

00:02:05.130 --> 00:02:10.840
is virtually impossible. So while we are winning
the ideological battle and while we are winning

00:02:10.840 --> 00:02:17.060
the support of so many young people and working
people throughout the country, I have concluded

00:02:17.060 --> 00:02:24.330
that this battle for the Democratic nomination
will not be successful. And so today I'm announcing

00:02:24.330 --> 00:02:30.540
the suspension of my campaign.
So, first of all, was this the correct decision

00:02:30.540 --> 00:02:36.099
for Bernie Sanders to make? The answer is
yes. Now, Bernie talks about the math and

00:02:36.099 --> 00:02:42.230
he realizes, he says, that he has no path
to the nomination. It's important to understand

00:02:42.230 --> 00:02:48.330
that it's been weeks since the numbers changed.
So if the numbers yesterday show no path to

00:02:48.330 --> 00:02:53.970
the nomination, he also had no path. Weeks
ago when we outlined that and still many people

00:02:53.970 --> 00:02:58.950
were reacting very emotionally and sort of
resisting that. After Super Tuesday, Bernie's

00:02:58.950 --> 00:03:05.190
shot was diminished to about a 1 percent shot
after the March 10th states voted. He had

00:03:05.190 --> 00:03:13.050
about a point, five percent chance after March
17th. It was smaller than a 0.1 percent chance.

00:03:13.050 --> 00:03:18.610
And that has not since changed. So Bernie's
decision is the right one. Bernie's decision

00:03:18.610 --> 00:03:24.269
is backed by the math, and there's no question
about that whatsoever. Remember, even after

00:03:24.269 --> 00:03:30.519
it was just Biden versus Bernie and everyone
else was out. Biden kept building bigger and

00:03:30.519 --> 00:03:35.260
bigger leads in the polls. There was the idea
that coronavirus would turn it around and

00:03:35.260 --> 00:03:41.299
reinvigorate Bernie's campaign in the polls.
Biden kept pulling away. So that's that. I

00:03:41.299 --> 00:03:45.989
don't really think there's that much more
to say about it, particularly because Bernie

00:03:45.989 --> 00:03:51.730
has suspended his campaign. Next question
is about the timing, Bernie getting out yesterday,

00:03:51.730 --> 00:03:57.980
April 8th, as opposed to earlier as opposed
to later. I don't know that this is the most

00:03:57.980 --> 00:04:03.190
important issue, but I'm not so sure about
the timing. I mean, to me, again, the numbers

00:04:03.190 --> 00:04:08.519
haven't changed for three weeks. So in a sense,
it might have made more sense to get out three

00:04:08.519 --> 00:04:16.140
weeks ago when we were not in the middle of
the peak of a hundred year pandemic, where

00:04:16.140 --> 00:04:21.020
this is likely to get it be a story that gets
24 to 36 hours of attention, and then the

00:04:21.020 --> 00:04:25.270
attention is going to be greatly diminished
waiting. I mean, listen, if you've waited

00:04:25.270 --> 00:04:30.720
this long, maybe you just keep waiting with
no other primaries that are voting in person

00:04:30.720 --> 00:04:35.450
in the immediate maybe you keep waiting with
the idea that when the virus starts to settle

00:04:35.450 --> 00:04:40.731
down in the news as hopefully it will in the
next month, although we don't know, maybe

00:04:40.731 --> 00:04:45.480
there's an opportunity for Bernie to get more
attention with this, get some concessions

00:04:45.480 --> 00:04:52.030
or something with Joe Biden, that will be
a show of both unity and maybe also some policy

00:04:52.030 --> 00:04:56.390
concessions that Joe Biden. I don't know.
I'm thinking out loud here, but I don't think

00:04:56.390 --> 00:05:02.500
this is really the most important thing. Might.
Instinct is that this is acutely a time because

00:05:02.500 --> 00:05:06.320
we are, you know, two thousand people a day
in the US or dying right now because of the

00:05:06.320 --> 00:05:11.380
Corona virus. This maybe is not the best time
to get the most attention for what you're

00:05:11.380 --> 00:05:16.050
doing and maybe spend the political capital
you've built in the most effective way. But

00:05:16.050 --> 00:05:20.390
I don't think it's the most important thing
to be talking about. Could maybe, Bernie,

00:05:20.390 --> 00:05:24.540
get something out of this in the future? Because
remember, Bernie is suspending. You can still

00:05:24.540 --> 00:05:29.490
vote for him in upcoming primaries. He will
continue to accumulate delegates. And at some

00:05:29.490 --> 00:05:34.530
point in the future, we imagine before or
at the convention, the convention maybe in

00:05:34.530 --> 00:05:38.400
person, it may be digital. We just don't know
right now because of the virus. Maybe there

00:05:38.400 --> 00:05:44.780
is some show made out of Bernie turning over
his delegates, directing his delegates, releasing

00:05:44.780 --> 00:05:49.430
his delegates and sending them to Biden in
exchange for something that may still happen.

00:05:49.430 --> 00:05:53.850
I don't know that we need to armchair quarterback
that, too, too much. Now let's move on to

00:05:53.850 --> 00:05:58.790
a bigger issue. What about the meaning of
this for the progressive movement and the

00:05:58.790 --> 00:06:03.270
understanding of why Bernie lost, which if
we don't learn anything from this, it's been

00:06:03.270 --> 00:06:09.080
a waste. If if we don't learn anything from
this, the same things are going to keep happening

00:06:09.080 --> 00:06:16.360
now. A lot of this analysis I've done before,
because we've already done our postmortem

00:06:16.360 --> 00:06:22.410
on the Bernie campaign mathematically in the
last three weeks, nothing changed. And Bernie,

00:06:22.410 --> 00:06:26.940
accepting that the math has no path to his
nomination. The math was the same three weeks

00:06:26.940 --> 00:06:31.970
ago. So we did most of our postmortem three
weeks ago. I won't go crazy spending time

00:06:31.970 --> 00:06:37.300
on that. But the key points to hit. Just so
we're all kind of up to speed. First of all,

00:06:37.300 --> 00:06:45.230
the Democratic primary electorate is not as
progressive as the Internet. Read it. Twitter.

00:06:45.230 --> 00:06:49.630
Progressive movement might make us think that
it is. This is just a reality. We talked about

00:06:49.630 --> 00:06:55.930
this a few weeks ago. There are a lot of Democratic
primary voters who just aren't participating

00:06:55.930 --> 00:07:00.370
in those online forums. So we don't see them.
We come away thinking that what we see on

00:07:00.370 --> 00:07:05.420
Reddit and Twitter is far more representative
of the Democratic primary electorate than

00:07:05.420 --> 00:07:12.030
it actually is. We sometimes are swayed by
Bernie's large rallies. Just because people

00:07:12.030 --> 00:07:16.820
are able to gather larger rallies doesn't
necessarily mean they're going to gather more

00:07:16.820 --> 00:07:21.740
voters when it actually becomes time to vote.
Now, you will hear on Twitter in response

00:07:21.740 --> 00:07:27.340
to this. You're wrong, David. Everybody wants
Medicare for all. Everybody wants free college.

00:07:27.340 --> 00:07:34.190
People were confused or tricked or bamboozled
into voting for Biden because of these wrong

00:07:34.190 --> 00:07:40.350
calculations about electability. People are
wrong. The theme on line is in the online

00:07:40.350 --> 00:07:48.690
left. It's Bernie is the guy with the popular
policies. But people wrongly thought Biden

00:07:48.690 --> 00:07:53.580
was more electable, so they voted for Biden.
That's not really true. And if you look at

00:07:53.580 --> 00:07:58.061
more detailed polls, you know, it's very easy
to say everybody loves Medicare for all, but

00:07:58.061 --> 00:08:03.750
somehow they voted for Biden. You know, it's
not completely true. And this is something

00:08:03.750 --> 00:08:07.750
if we don't accept, if we don't realize it,
we're not going to fix the problems. If you

00:08:07.750 --> 00:08:14.500
look at data from the Kaiser Family Foundation,
it's pretty clear. I want a disclaimer. Kaiser

00:08:14.500 --> 00:08:18.741
Family Foundation has nothing to do with Kaiser
Permanente, the insurance company. Sometimes

00:08:18.741 --> 00:08:24.030
when I mentioned the K F F people say, David,
you're touting industry talking points. No,

00:08:24.030 --> 00:08:28.550
the Kaiser Family Foundation. You can look
up, Google it. It's widely documented. It

00:08:28.550 --> 00:08:34.430
shares the word Kaiser. It has nothing to
do with the insurance company Kaiser Permanente.

00:08:34.430 --> 00:08:39.330
They're an independent research agency. And
the point is, the more you tell people about

00:08:39.330 --> 00:08:43.860
Medicare for all and how it would actually
work, the lower support is. Now, this doesn't

00:08:43.860 --> 00:08:47.701
mean Medicare for all is good or bad. I'm
talking about the political viability. We

00:08:47.701 --> 00:08:52.280
have some of the data on the screen. This
is not anything about my opinion. It is simply

00:08:52.280 --> 00:08:57.190
me reminding you the numbers are more complex
than simply saying everybody loves Medicare

00:08:57.190 --> 00:09:01.890
for all. But somehow Biden won by two and
a half million votes. The more you tell people

00:09:01.890 --> 00:09:06.711
about the specifics of how Medicare for all
would work, the more divided opinion is. It's

00:09:06.711 --> 00:09:12.080
not overwhelmingly against Medicare for all,
but opinion about Medicare for all is split

00:09:12.080 --> 00:09:18.000
very evenly as people learn more about the
specifics. So it's not overwhelming support

00:09:18.000 --> 00:09:25.810
number two, policy aside. Not enough people
liked Bernie enough to vote for him. This

00:09:25.810 --> 00:09:29.710
is not the Hillary stuff. Nobody likes Bernie.
That was referring to members of Congress

00:09:29.710 --> 00:09:35.750
in the Senate. What I'm talking about is there
are lots of people who I'm sure find Bernie's

00:09:35.750 --> 00:09:43.060
policies fine, but they didn't like him or
his campaign enough to get them over the hump,

00:09:43.060 --> 00:09:48.280
casting a ballot for Bernie Sanders. Now,
there are all of these hot takes that Bernie

00:09:48.280 --> 00:09:55.010
lost because voters were confused about issues
vs. electability. But a lot of people just

00:09:55.010 --> 00:09:59.420
didn't like Bernie enough to vote for him.
It's just the reality. OK, I don't take it.

00:09:59.420 --> 00:10:04.400
Personally, it has nothing to do with the
viability of the policies either. Number three,

00:10:04.400 --> 00:10:08.510
I've already talked about the toxic people
around Bernie. There are lots of them. This

00:10:08.510 --> 00:10:12.080
isn't about mean people on Twitter. That's
not what I'm talking about. I'm talking about

00:10:12.080 --> 00:10:18.140
campaign surrogates. It wouldn't be particularly
particularly decorous for me to start naming

00:10:18.140 --> 00:10:23.400
them. Is it decorous or de chorus for me to
start naming them down? Now it's over. But

00:10:23.400 --> 00:10:27.610
there are lots of people around, Bernie, that
were repellent to many, many voters. It was

00:10:27.610 --> 00:10:32.970
a bad calculation. What can you do? OK, we
learned. And lastly, Bernie was not helped

00:10:32.970 --> 00:10:37.800
by some of the optics around his campaign.
The Democratic Socialist label didn't help.

00:10:37.800 --> 00:10:42.660
I said this five years ago and there are now
more and more leftist folks who are coming

00:10:42.660 --> 00:10:49.420
around to this. It just didn't help thinking
about it. It's not anything personal, personal,

00:10:49.420 --> 00:10:55.390
personal. About Bernie necessarily. But the
Dems socialist language, the language of revolution.

00:10:55.390 --> 00:11:00.010
Most Democrats don't want revolution. They
want to fix the system. And even, you know,

00:11:00.010 --> 00:11:04.650
this is so minor. But like when Bernie praised
Cuba's literacy program and then doubled down

00:11:04.650 --> 00:11:10.800
on it. I get it. Just because Cuba did something
doesn't mean that Fidel Castro is good, but

00:11:10.800 --> 00:11:15.620
it just didn't help, Bernie. None of this
stuff helped Bernie Sanders. All together,

00:11:15.620 --> 00:11:20.500
many factors. So then we get to does this
say anything about the future of the progressive

00:11:20.500 --> 00:11:25.410
movement more broadly? I think the answer
is not necessarily. It depends on the choices

00:11:25.410 --> 00:11:31.010
that we make. I've said before the movement
to succeed is going to be a need to be led

00:11:31.010 --> 00:11:39.350
by someone who shares Bernie's fundamental
values, but has better optics, better framing,

00:11:39.350 --> 00:11:45.480
better language and a less toxic supporting
cast around them. There's plenty of time to

00:11:45.480 --> 00:11:48.760
figure that out. We want to take too much
time because we want to make progress and

00:11:48.760 --> 00:11:53.830
win. But there's plenty of time to figure
that out. But in the immediate, in the midst

00:11:53.830 --> 00:12:00.110
of 100 year pandemic during which the president
we have is an incompetent, weaponized buffoon,

00:12:00.110 --> 00:12:04.850
we've got to deal with the general election.
This is not trivial. This is not academic.

00:12:04.850 --> 00:12:10.930
And this is where the black white hot takes
are just exploding on the Internet, probably

00:12:10.930 --> 00:12:15.450
to the detriment of the movement. Bigger picture
because everybody is claiming to have the

00:12:15.450 --> 00:12:21.120
perspective that informs what every Bernie
supporter should do in November. You've got

00:12:21.120 --> 00:12:25.960
the never Biden people. You've got the Bernie
or bust people, which are not necessarily

00:12:25.960 --> 00:12:32.500
the same as the never Biden people. You have
the reluctant sort of trumps better than Biden.

00:12:32.500 --> 00:12:40.279
But I hate him anyway. People. Here's my suggestion.
Let's stop. Let's be adults here. And I'll

00:12:40.279 --> 00:12:44.970
explain to you what I mean by that. Bernie,
supporters have a limited number of options.

00:12:44.970 --> 00:12:49.560
It's not there's not an unlimited number of
paths forward. And those are you vote for

00:12:49.560 --> 00:12:57.020
Biden. You vote for Trump. You don't vote
at all. You write, Bernie in talking in November.

00:12:57.020 --> 00:13:03.029
Now you write someone else in or you vote
for a third party candidate. These are all

00:13:03.029 --> 00:13:10.160
different actions. But in practical terms,
any of these actions other than voting Biden

00:13:10.160 --> 00:13:15.520
is an action that gets Trump one vote closer
to reelection. That's not a value judgment.

00:13:15.520 --> 00:13:20.029
I'm not saying it's good or bad. We'll get
to the values in a moment. But any decision

00:13:20.029 --> 00:13:25.500
other than a vote for Biden is a vote or a
non vote that helps Donald Trump. Now, you

00:13:25.500 --> 00:13:31.440
know, in blue states where Biden will win,
maybe in practice it matters less what you

00:13:31.440 --> 00:13:37.670
do in terms of helping Trump. But at the national
level, all choices other than voting Biden

00:13:37.670 --> 00:13:43.040
are a vote that helps Trump get closer to
reelection. Now, people may have different

00:13:43.040 --> 00:13:48.160
reasons for choosing these options. So as
an example, you might be a Bernie supporter

00:13:48.160 --> 00:13:52.390
and you might choose to vote for Trump because
you actually preferred Trump to Biden. Like

00:13:52.390 --> 00:13:57.820
on policy, I guess it's conceivable you could
look at the policy and you could look at everything

00:13:57.820 --> 00:14:01.751
about them, the people around them, cabinets
that they would. Okay. And you say, I prefer

00:14:01.751 --> 00:14:06.020
Trump to Biden. That's one reason someone
might vote for Trump over Biden. You might

00:14:06.020 --> 00:14:11.029
be a Bernie supporter and you might vote for
Trump because you see Trump's reelection as

00:14:11.029 --> 00:14:17.060
acceleration ist compared to a Biden win.
And now acceleration ism is the idea that

00:14:17.060 --> 00:14:22.570
you should accelerate capitalism because it
will speed up its eventual failure, which

00:14:22.570 --> 00:14:28.750
will bring about the destruction of capitalism.
That's an idea you might choose. Any of these

00:14:28.750 --> 00:14:35.450
options other than voting Biden because you
want to teach the DNC a lesson and you see

00:14:35.450 --> 00:14:40.540
not voting for Biden as teaching the D and
see a lesson that, you know, your vote is

00:14:40.540 --> 00:14:46.550
not a blank check. So here's where I come
down on this. I cannot in good conscience

00:14:46.550 --> 00:14:53.670
take any action that will make Trump's reelection
more likely. It's very simple for me. I believe

00:14:53.670 --> 00:14:59.110
that Trump is that bad. I believe the Corona
virus epidemic has been sort of. The straw

00:14:59.110 --> 00:15:03.490
that broke the camel's back or the cherry
on top or whatever metaphor you want to use

00:15:03.490 --> 00:15:10.080
that proves beyond any doubt how weaponized
Trump's ignorance and personality disorders

00:15:10.080 --> 00:15:16.840
and bad ideas and cast of supporters and staffers
are. This is not vote blue no matter who for

00:15:16.840 --> 00:15:22.930
me. I have a video about this on YouTube you
can check out. I've looked at the options

00:15:22.930 --> 00:15:28.561
and I am choosing Biden over Trump because
he's better. OK. Yesterday on Twitter, our

00:15:28.561 --> 00:15:33.980
friend Kyle Kolinsky responded to journalist
medi- Hassans tweet about the lesser of two

00:15:33.980 --> 00:15:40.570
evils. And Kyle said, OK, white nationalist
Richard Spencer versus white nationalist David

00:15:40.570 --> 00:15:48.029
Duke, who y'all got? And I responded, half
joking, but half serious, I guess. David Duke,

00:15:48.029 --> 00:15:53.540
he seems more frail and his supporters aren't
as good at using the Internet to spread their

00:15:53.540 --> 00:16:00.110
white nationalism. The point here is I believe
in harm reduction. I reject the idea that

00:16:00.110 --> 00:16:04.901
acceleration ism will succeed at toppling
the system. When you look at history, you

00:16:04.901 --> 00:16:09.411
see that the big progressive advances, which
were, you know, in the last hundred and so

00:16:09.411 --> 00:16:16.540
years, the 1910 to 1920 progressive era, the
New Deal era and the civil rights era, those

00:16:16.540 --> 00:16:23.399
were not revolution. Break the system and
build it back up, burn it down and start over.

00:16:23.399 --> 00:16:27.980
Those were advances working within the system
and improving the system. Now, there is another

00:16:27.980 --> 00:16:34.070
group that is talking about, you know, Biden
needs to earn my vote. The DNC needs to earn

00:16:34.070 --> 00:16:37.620
my vote. They need to come and get me. And
unless they come and get me, unless they make

00:16:37.620 --> 00:16:43.760
overtures and come and get me, they don't
deserve my vote. Another debate is, is it

00:16:43.760 --> 00:16:49.090
Bernie? Who needs to convince his supporters
to vote for Biden? Or is it Biden who needs

00:16:49.090 --> 00:16:54.270
to convince Bernie's supporters to vote for
Biden? This entire thing is childish to me.

00:16:54.270 --> 00:17:00.990
This idea of who comes and gets me specifically
strikes me as both childish and completely

00:17:00.990 --> 00:17:06.670
irrelevant. I don't care about these people
as people. I don't DFI politicians. I've expressed

00:17:06.670 --> 00:17:12.400
before, you know, that the deification of
Bernie or Tulsi or Andrew Gang or Trump, it's

00:17:12.400 --> 00:17:18.559
all cultish. And I just don't think these
are people that should be deified or revered

00:17:18.559 --> 00:17:22.980
in this way. They're just people. They're
just people. They're flawed people. I don't

00:17:22.980 --> 00:17:27.700
agree with everything in their platforms,
period. I don't care about the cult of personality

00:17:27.700 --> 00:17:33.040
around them. I don't care about them coming
to get my vote. I'm not signing a blank check.

00:17:33.040 --> 00:17:39.920
I look at policy and Biden is better. I'm
not arrogant enough to say Biden's gotta come

00:17:39.920 --> 00:17:45.340
get my vote. I've looked at Biden versus Trump
on health care. Biden's better. Biden the

00:17:45.340 --> 00:17:51.260
best. No. Biden's better. I've looked at Biden
versus Trump on taxes. Biden's better. I've

00:17:51.260 --> 00:17:56.559
looked at Biden versus Trump on selecting
judges. Biden is better. I've looked at them

00:17:56.559 --> 00:18:00.720
on the environment. I've looked at them on
diplomacy. I've looked at just about every

00:18:00.720 --> 00:18:05.929
issue. And Biden is better. I'm a big boy.
I don't need Biden to come kowtow to me or

00:18:05.929 --> 00:18:12.050
do anything like that to get my votes. I've
done the analysis on my own, and I know what

00:18:12.050 --> 00:18:16.590
the right decision is here. I'm not going
to attack people who are going to go a different

